=== Agreement ===
CFA released to reach partial invariance: none (full scalar passes) 
IRT flagged (purified anchor):      4 Low energy;  5 Appetite change;  7 Trouble concentrating;  8 Psychomotor change;  9 Suicidal ideation 
IRT flagged at every anchor size:   4,5,9  (item numbers)

Both methods: none 

Spearman correlation of the two rankings, over the 5 items the IRT
side tested: +0.60. With 5 points this is descriptive, not a test;
it is here to show the direction of agreement, not to certify it.

=== The somatic reading ===
The standing claim in this literature is that somatic items (sleep,
energy, appetite, psychomotor) are what make the PHQ-9 behave differently
across sex. Both methods get asked whether they support it.

CFA: mean score statistic, somatic 14.6 vs non-somatic 10.7
IRT: 3 of 5 flagged items are somatic (4 of 9 items are)
IRT: 2 flagged items have a negative SIDS, meaning they under-report
     for women at equal depression:
       4 Low energy             -0.064 pts  somatic TRUE
       5 Appetite change        -0.050 pts  somatic TRUE

=== Reading this honestly ===
On random splits of this same sample the anchored IRT procedure
flags an item 1.3% of the time with nothing there, and 7% of
splits produce at least one flag. The agreement above has to clear
that bar before it means the two methods found the same real thing
rather than the same artifact.

